{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966801,"nonce":"ZzpqKPZku6gh24jFac2Hbwj486Q=","title":"Rich text ignored its own wrap:true — the named culprit was dead code, and the real fix","message":"`RichText` silently ignored `wrap: true`. Long paragraphs overflowed\ninstead of breaking. Three separate causes, and the one recorded in the\npinned test's comment was wrong.\n\n**The wrong lead.** `blinc_gpu::text::prepare_styled_text` does hardcode\n`LineBreakMode::None` and pass no `max_width`, which reads like the\ncause. **It has no callers anywhere in the repo.** Rich text is painted\nby the `ElementType::StyledText` arm of `collect_elements` in\n`blinc_app`'s context, which emits one `TextElement` per style segment\nand lays them out left-to-right with a running `x_offset`. Grep for the\nconsumer before trusting a function that merely looks responsible.\n\n**1. Sizing.** `RichText::build` called `create_node`, so the node got a\nfixed width from an unwrapped measurement. Plain text (`text.rs`) uses\n`create_text_node` with a `TextMeasureContext`, which is how taffy gets\nto ask \"how tall at this width?\". Rich text now does the same, and\n`update_size_estimate` leaves width/height `Auto` when wrapping, exactly\nas the plain-text path does.\n\n**2. Painting.** The segment loop had one running `x_offset` and no\nconcept of a line. It now walks `text_line_spans` for the node's\nlaid-out width, clips each style segment to the line being drawn, and\nresets `x_offset` per line. A segment straddling a wrap point is drawn\nas two runs. Per-run `height` stays the node height when there is one\nline (preserving existing vertical centring) and becomes the line band\nwhen wrapped.\n\n**3. A latent bug wrapping would have exposed.** `prepare_styled_text`\nin `blinc_text` mapped the *nth glyph* to the *nth char index* to pick\nits colour. That holds only while glyph order matches char order 1:1 —\nwhich wrapping breaks, because the break drops whitespace glyphs. Every\nspan colour after the first wrap point would have shifted. Fixed by\ncarrying the shaper's cluster through `PositionedGlyph.byte_offset` and\nreading that instead.\n\n**A test that passed for the wrong reason.** The pinned\n`rich_text_does_not_wrap_yet` compared heights of a rich text child in a\n`div().w(w).h(400.0)`. The child stretched to the cross axis, so both\nheights were 400 whatever the text did — it would have passed after\nwrapping landed too. Cross-axis stretch defeats any height assertion:\nuse `items_start()`. Once fixed the numbers are stark, 17px at 1200px vs\n101px at 200px.\n\nRelated: [[gotcha-hover-cursor-six-gates]] for the link-geometry half,\nwhich had to land in the same change.","files":null}]}